            { text: "Thus, there being four magnitudes, namely two bases {CB} and {CD}, and two triangles {ACB} and {ACD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CB","CD","ABC","ACD"] },
            { text: "equimultiples have been taken of the base {CB} and the triangle {ACB}, namely the base {CH} and the triangle {ACH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH","ACH"] },
            { text: "and other, arbitrary, equimultiples of the base {CD} and the triangle {ADC}, namely the base {CL} and the triangle {ACL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL","ACL"] },
            { text: "and it has been proved that, if the base {CH} is in excess of the base {CL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH","CL"] },
            { text: "the triangle {ACH} is also in excess of the triangle {ACL}; if equal, equal; and, if less, less.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ACH","ACL"] },
            { text: "Therefore the base {CB} is to the base {CD} as the triangle {ACB} is to the triangle {ACD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CB","CD","ABC","ACD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "the definition of same ratio", ref: "V.Def.5" }] },
            { text: "Next, since the parallelogram {CE} is double the triangle {ACB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CE","ABC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a parallelogram is double the triangle on its base", ref: "I.41" }] },
            { text: "and the parallelogram {FC} is double the triangle {ACD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF","ACD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.41" }] },
            { text: "and parts have the same ratio as their equimultiples,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CE","CF","ABC","ACD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "parts have the same ratio as their equimultiples", ref: "V.15" }] },
            { text: "therefore the triangle {ACB} is to the triangle {ACD} as the parallelogram {CE} is to the parallelogram {FC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABC","ACD","CE","CF"] },
            { text: "Since, then, it was proved that the base {CB} is to {CD} as the triangle {ACB} is to the triangle {ACD},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CB","CD","ABC","ACD"] },
            { text: "and the triangle {ACB} is to the triangle {ACD} as the parallelogram {CE} is to the parallelogram {CF},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABC","ACD","CE","CF"] },
            { text: "therefore also the base {CB} is to the base {CD} as the parallelogram {CE} is to the parallelogram {FC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CB","CD","CE","CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "ratios the same as the same ratio", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, triangles and parallelograms which are under the same height are to one another as their bases.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["ABC","ACD","CE","CF","CB","CD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.1") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.2": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "I.3":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.38":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI38/",
        "I.41":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI41/",
        "V.Def.5":  "/elements/books/bookV/definitions/defV5/",
        "V.11":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "V.15":     "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV15/"
